# Another program rewrites a note while the delete prompt is open: y doesn't delete it but asks
# again, about the new version. n leaves it as they wrote it. Asked afresh, y sends that version
# to the trash and u puts it back. tests/drive.rs checks the file and the trash.
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
keys p lava
wait-for Lava
keys enter
wait-for Concepts/Lava  reading
keys d
wait-for Delete Concepts/Lava?
write Concepts/Lava.md Rewritten in Obsidian while the prompt was open.\n
keys y
wait-for ! It changed on disk since you asked: this is the new version.
expect Delete Concepts/Lava?
expect example-workspace 35 notes
keys n
wait-for delete cancelled
expect example-workspace 35 notes
keys d
wait-for Delete Concepts/Lava?
expect-not It changed on disk
keys y
wait-for deleted Lava · u undo
wait-for example-workspace 34 notes
keys u
wait-for restored Concepts/Lava.md
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
wait-for Concepts/Lava  reading
expect Rewritten in Obsidian while the prompt was open.
keys esc
wait-for ? help  q quit
keys q
exits 0
